Logic :

 traverse the array only once while maintaining the current prefix sum. At every index,  check whether there was a previous prefix sum equal to currentPrefix - k. 
If it exists, then the elements between that previous position and the current position form a subarray with sum k.
Since the same prefix sum can occur multiple times, store its frequency in a HashMap and add that frequency to my answer.
Finally, Istore the current prefix sum in the map and continue.

Code :

class Solution {
    public int subarraySum(int[] nums, int k) {
        int prefix=0;
        int c=0;
        HashMap<Integer,Integer> map=new HashMap<>();
        map.put(0,1);
        for(int num:nums){
            prefix+=num;
            if(map.containsKey(prefix-k)){
                c+=map.get(prefix-k);
            }
            map.put(prefix,map.getOrDefault(prefix,0)+1);
        }
        return c;
    }
}
